    {
      "text": "to mock, and to scourge, and to crucify him, Matt. 20:19 (2 Ne. 6:9; Mosiah 3:9). Son of man is betrayed to be crucified, Matt. 26:2. Let him be crucified, Matt. 27:22 (Luke 23:23). they crucified him, Matt. 27:35 (Mark 15:15; John 19:16). ye seek Jesus, which was crucified, Matt. 28:5 (Mark 16:6). Son of man … must suffer many things, and be set at nought, Mark 9:12 (9:31). cried out again, Crucify him, Mark 15:13 (John 19:6, 15). Calvary, there they crucified him, Luke 23:33. condemned to death, and have crucified him, Luke 24:20. if I be lifted up from the earth, John 12:32 (1 Ne. 11:33; 19:10; Moses 7:55). knowest thou not that I have power to crucify, John 19:10. bodies should not remain upon the cross, John 19:31 (Deut. 21:23). I shall see in his hands the print of the nails, John 20:25. by wicked hands have crucified and slain, Acts 2:23 (Mosiah 15:7). same Jesus, whom ye have crucified, Acts 2:36. whom ye crucified, whom God raised from the dead, Acts 4:10. Jesus, whom ye slew and hanged on a tree, Acts 5:30. we preach Christ crucified, 1 Cor. 1:23. not to know any thing … save Jesus Christ, and him crucified, 1 Cor. 2:2. they would not have crucified the Lord, 1 Cor. 2:8. though he was crucified through weakness, 2 Cor. 13:4. world is crucified unto me, Gal. 6:14. crucify to themselves the Son of God afresh, Heb. 6:6. where also our Lord was crucified, Rev. 11:8.",
